course: dictionary
lesson: 10040
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word terrace can mean a flat place to sit, a row of houses, steps on a hill, or the steps where fans stand at a football match. You can work out which one is meant by reading the words around it. These words are its context.
explain: «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes.» Hilly places and slopes are the clues, so terraces here must be flat steps on a hillside. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «In Leeds, the family lived in a terraced house.» Here Leeds is a town, and a terraced house is a house joined to the houses either side of it in a row. The context tells you the meaning, and a dictionary confirms it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Terrace» can mean a flat area next to a house, café or hotel where people sit outside.
fact: In the UK, a terrace is a row of houses joined together in a line.
fact: A terrace can also be one of a set of flat steps cut into a hillside for growing crops, such as «rice terraces» in Asia.
fact: «Terraces» can also mean the wide steps in a sports ground where fans stand to watch, and «terrace» is used this way in the UK and Ireland.
exercise: «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes.» What are terraces here? | A row of houses joined together | *Flat steps cut into a hillside for growing crops | Wide steps where fans stand at a football ground | A flat area outside a café where people sit
exercise: «The fans stood on the terraces, singing all afternoon.» Where did the fans stand? | *Wide steps in a sports ground | A row of houses in a line | Flat steps on a hillside for crops | A flat area next to a café
exercise: «Mum and Dad sat on the roof terrace to watch the sunset.» Find and copy the word that tells you where they sat. | watch | *terrace | sunset | roof
test: «In Leeds, the family lived in a terraced house.» What does terraced house mean? | A house with a flat roof where people can sit | *A house joined in a row to the houses on either side | A house built on a steep hill with steps down to the road | A house with a big garden at the back
test: «The rice terraces stop soil being washed away.» Why are rice terraces useful? | They join houses together in a line | They make a flat place for parties on a roof | *They stop soil washing away and give flat ground for farming | They give fans a place to stand and watch
exam: Which meaning fits terrace in «We ate lunch on the café terrace in the sunshine»? | Flat steps cut into a hillside for crops | A row of houses joined together | Wide steps where fans stand at a sports ground | *A flat area outside where people can sit
